<div class="create-segment-form-wrapper" id="new-segment-div">
  <div class="content-sub-wrapper modal w-clearfix">
    <h4 class="modal-header welcome-dash-content-container-header">Create Segment</h4>
    <a class="close-modal update-close-modals" data-parent="new-segment-div" href="#" ></a>
  </div>
  <p class="modal-content-description">A segment is a group (subset) of your customers defined by filters that you set. Customers that match these filters are automatically added to the group over time.</p>
  <div class="create-segment w-form">
    <%= form_for('lists', url: v1_lists_path, html: { id: "create_segment" }) do |f| %>
      <label class="form-label list-name" for="Segment-Name-2">Segment name</label>
      <%= f.hidden_field :list_type, value: 'segment' %>
      <%= f.hidden_field :segment_type, id: 'segment_type' %>
      <%= f.hidden_field :segment_num_days, id: 'segment_num_days' %>
      <%= f.hidden_field :segment_filter, id: 'segment_filter' %>
      <%= f.hidden_field :amt_filter, id: 'amt_filter' %>
      <%= f.hidden_field :amt_1, id: 'lists_amt_1' %>
      <%= f.hidden_field :amt_2, id: 'lists_amt_2' %>
      <div class='form-group col-xs-6'>
        <%= f.text_field :segment_name, class: 'form-control segment-name text-field w-input' %>
      </div>
      <%= f.submit 'Create Segment', class: 'button create-segment-button w-button' %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <p class="modal-paragraph segment tips"> &nbsp;TIP: You can setup automated drip campaigns to nurture customers or leads. First create segments for each key group of customers or leads, E.g:leads that became customers 3-6 days ago,followed by leads that became customers 7-14 days ago, etc. Then go to your campaigns page to set up automatic messages.</p>
  <%= link_to 'Manage segments', segments_user_path(current_user), class: 'button manage-segments w-button' %>
</div>
